<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-CN">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>About Bazi</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
</head>
<body class="about-page">

  <!-- Navbar -->
  <nav class="navbar">
    <a href="/result">Today's Drink</a>
    <a href="/previous">History</a>
    <a href="/about" class="active">About Project</a>
    <a href="/logout">Logout</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- hint -->
  <section id="hero">
    <div class="scroll-hint">↓ Scroll Down</div>
  </section>

 
<section id="arch-section">
    <div class="arch-content">
      <div class="slogan">
        <h1>Unlocking the Energy in Your Birth</h1>
        <p>Understand the ancient wisdom behind your daily drink ritual</p>
      </div>
      
  <!-- inforamtion of the project -->
  <section class="info-blocks">
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>What is Bazi?</strong>
      <p>
        “Bazi” (八字) translates to “Eight Characters” — a system rooted in traditional Chinese metaphysics.
        These eight characters are derived from your exact birth date and time, each pairing a “Heavenly Stem” and an “Earthly Branch.”
        Together, they form a unique energetic blueprint that reflects your personality, strengths, challenges, and the cyclical rhythms of your life.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>How is it Calculated?</strong>
      <p>
        We begin by converting your Gregorian birthdate and hour into the traditional Chinese lunar calendar.
        This yields four pillars — year, month, day, and hour — each composed of one stem and one branch.
        The resulting “Eight Characters” (two from each pillar) correspond to the Five Elements (Wood, Fire, Earth, Metal, Water),
        allowing us to assess balance and energy flow within your life chart.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>Traditional Applications</strong>
      <p>
        Bazi is commonly used to interpret one’s fate, predict fortune cycles, and offer guidance on relationships, health, and career.
        For centuries, people have used Bazi to identify auspicious dates for weddings, business launches, or even house moves —
        all by aligning personal energy with cosmic rhythms.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>How We Use Bazi Here</strong>
      <p>
        We analyze your Bazi chart to identify elemental imbalances — for example, whether you lack Water or have an excess of Fire.
        These insights help us match you with ingredients associated with the elements you need most that day.
        Each drink recommendation is a ritual for energetic alignment — harmonizing your inner landscape through flavor, temperature, 
        and Five Element symbolism.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>



  <script>
    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      const arch = document.getElementById('arch-section');
      const scrollHint = document.querySelector('.scroll-hint');
      const triggerPoint = window.innerHeight * 0.3;
  
      // Show the arch when scrolled past trigger point
      if (window.scrollY > triggerPoint) {
        arch.classList.add('visible');
      } else {
        arch.classList.remove('visible');
      }
  
      // Hide scroll hint when scrolling down
      if (window.scrollY > 50) {
        scrollHint.style.opacity = '0';
        scrollHint.style.pointerEvents = 'none';
      } else {
        scrollHint.style.opacity = '1';
        scrollHint.style.pointerEvents = 'auto';
      }
    });
  </script>
  
  
</body>
</html>
